//! Native state and storage for the pinned QuickJS engine; no evaluator or runtime policy.
//!
//! Every JS reference below is explicit: copying ValueBits or a raw header pointer does not
//! retain it. HeapHeader is the only JS reference count. Native container destruction
//! releases storage, NOT the JS children it contains; engine destruction must visit and
//! release those children first. List length/capacity replace the source's count/size pairs.
//!
//! Heap pointers name HeapCell payloads of the documented type. Only HeapCell.payload /
//! payloadMut may recover them: neither header offsets nor native struct layout are ABI.
//! Raw links are borrowed and require live, stable allocations and exclusive mutation.
//! RuntimeAllocator and reentrant host dispatch providers belong to the public Runtime
//! handle, not RuntimeState; source malloc bookkeeping is provided by runtime_memory.

